  "source_review_observations": [
    "Source-only helper flavors statically select API28 target28 legacy; API29 target28 default legacy, target29 explicit legacy and scoped; API30 target35 normal and exceptional allFiles.",
    "Compiled helper predicates require exactly selected SDK/flavor/storage permissions, one signature control, DUMP/UID2000-only cleanup provider, no grant/path cleanup ingress, and exact private signer min=max=actual route API.",
    "Reporter compiled predicates require the exact library AndroidJUnitRunner/min23/target37 package, no native storage permission, and a MANAGE_DOCUMENTS-protected grantUriPermissions provider.",
    "Each native request verifies actual helper/reporter installed APK/certificate, unsplit state, separate normal UID and PID, package ownership, SDK/target/flavor, exact nonce and Binder sender identity.",
    "Protected file operations execute in the ordinary helper UID using O_EXCL and 257-byte payload, exact SHA-256, EOF, descriptor-close invalidation, exclusive owned unlink/ENOENT and only EACCES/EPERM denials.",
    "API28 legacy WRITE is explicitly native-granted for the test; API29 NotRequired helper never supplies that native prerequisite. Scoped storage remains bounded even with the separate native WRITE grant.",
